{
 "summary": "Checkout failures originate in inventory: starting 2s after inventory was deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.2 (07:23:48Z), inventory began logging 'connection pool exhausted' and returning 500 on POST /reserve, which propagates as 502 through orders and gateway. Failures are fast (8-26ms), not timeouts, and inventory's 5xx ratio peaks around 51%. The inventory 3.2.2 deploy is the leading suspect; rolling it back is the most direct mitigation.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory release 3.2.2, deployed at 07:23:48Z, exhausts its connection pool, so POST /reserve returns 500. Orders and gateway pass that failure on as 502. The deploy is linked to the errors by timing (errors start 2s later), by every error log and sampled trace carrying release 3.2.2, and by the error originating at inventory. That the code change itself causes the exhaustion is inferred, not directly shown.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-496b376605a8",
   "ev-c8ce64f94212",
   "ev-31f2c154a94c",
   "ev-3cebf0e05abb"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders and gateway have no fallback for inventory reservation failures. Each inventory 500 becomes an orders 502 and then a gateway 502 on checkout, with matching counts (92) in all three services' error logs.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-3a77f4276cd1",
    "ev-16f53b9d12b3",
    "ev-c8ce64f94212",
    "ev-31f2c154a94c"
   ]
  }
 ],
