    "ev-bc2db81f526d",
    "ev-eb1a06578431"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "A latency or timeout cascade. p95 latency never crossed its onset threshold in any service (inventory max 46ms), and failing traces complete in 8-26ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-3cebf0e05abb",
    "ev-bc2db81f526d",
    "ev-eb1a06578431",
    "ev-31f2c154a94c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway or orders as the origin. Both only report downstream failures ('orders returned 502', 'inventory reservation failed with status 500'). The deepest failing span is inventory POST /reserve with 500.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-16f53b9d12b3",
    "ev-3a77f4276cd1",
    "ev-31f2c154a94c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "A traffic surge exhausting the pool. Request rates stay low: inventory averages 1.18 req/s and peaks at 1.54.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-3cebf0e05abb"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "What changed in inventory 3.2.2: pool size or config, connection leaks, or a new dependency.",
  "Which backend the exhausted pool connects to (e.g. a database), and whether that backend's metrics or logs show problems. No evidence on it was collected.",
  "Inventory metrics from before the deploy, to confirm a clean baseline under 3.1.5.",
  "Why only about half of inventory requests fail. This could be partial rollout, per-instance pools, or gradual leak behavior.",
  "Whether 'intermittently' in the incident title refers to failures before 07:23:48 that fall outside this evidence."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Roll back inventory to 3.1.5.",
   "rationale": "Errors began 2s after the 3.2.2 deploy and all failures originate in inventory 3.2.2 with pool exhaustion.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-496b376605a8",
    "ev-c8ce64f94212"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "After the rollback, confirm the inventory, orders and gateway 5xx ratios drop below 5%.",
   "rationale": "This validates the deploy hypothesis, since all three error ratios moved together.",
